In the prey equation $dot(x) = alpha x - beta x^2 - gamma x y$, the term $alpha x$ models excess births over natural deaths, $beta x^2$ competition over scarce resources, and $gamma x y$ deaths due to predation. In the predator equation $dot(y) = epsilon x y - delta y$, the birth rate increases with predation while $delta y$ is the natural death rate. All of $alpha, beta, gamma, delta, epsilon$ are positive constants.
